# fixedbugs, defect 232, lane b8-ffi, 2026-10-03.
#
# The group's header is on this machine and includes one that is not, named
# with a `'`. The reader of clang's *'...' file not found* cut the name at
# its first quote, so the message said `fixedbugs-232-gone` was missing, a
# name nothing includes. It reads the name up to the line's last
# *' file not found* now. A program `check` passes reaches this shape, where
# a `'` in the group's own header is refused at `check` (panel 188's R4); the
# reader of that one is held by `emit/ffi_build.hero`'s unit test.

extern "fixedbugs-232-includes-a-header-named-with-a-quote.h"
    function seven() -> i32  #~ ffi_missing_header

function main()
    print(seven())
